- **Headline takeaway for report**: NotebookLM is the **lightweight QA tool** of the lineup — fastest by far (UC01 ~30 s), zero-fabrication discipline, but breaks down on larger corpora. Not a fit for high-volume DDQs against a 25+ doc corpus.
- **Time**: **~15 minutes total workflow.** NotebookLM's chat UI caps per-turn submissions at 10–25 questions, so the 100-question run required 5–10 separate chat turns. Per-question rate is ~1–2 minutes across the workflow (generation per batch is fast, but turn boundaries dominate wall-clock). **This is a real UX constraint for high-volume DDQs** — even at NotebookLM's lightweight throughput, the per-turn cap means a 100-Q questionnaire needs operator orchestration vs Normain's single-shot run.

